Paste the draft and I'll review it against the standards we've discussed:

1. Whether the access question is argued on authorization grounds alone, with no reliance on what the data showed;
2. Whether the decoupling is stated explicitly rather than implied;
3. Whether the finding keeps its hedges ("suggests," "pending the vendor's methodology") rather than asserting the vendor's number is wrong;
4. Whether anything concedes the access was unauthorized before the panel has ruled;
5. Whether the finding is framed as a routing request (to the contract owner, via authorized re-pull) rather than a conclusion you want the panel to adopt.

One thing before you paste: you still haven't said whether the logs came through your normal system credentials or access outside your designated role. If the draft asserts the access was authorized, I need that answer to evaluate whether the assertion holds — a statement at the hearing that doesn't survive a follow-up question is worse than a narrower one that does.
